 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch17_04_01\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-id2009548\" data-alt=\"The PCA3 test occurs in three steps. In step one, PCA3 mRNA anneals to complementary DNA primers that are attached to beads. In step two, the mRNA is amplified using reverse-transcriptase PCR. In step three, the mRNA is detected using a chemiluminescent probe.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20210823.155019/resources/31ac7a3907e1490023963bdccf37de646bf89bbd\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"The PCA3 test occurs in three steps. In step one, PCA3 mRNA anneals to complementary DNA primers that are attached to beads. In step two, the mRNA is amplified using reverse-transcriptase PCR. In step three, the mRNA is detected using a chemiluminescent probe.\" width=\"325\" id=\"3\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 639815,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/858a99e4f31ca490.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Kumar, Ravinder, and Pradeep Kumar/National Center for Biotechnology Information, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>Using microbes to convert sugars into fuels is a developing field of study. The table gives some organisms studied in such research and also shows how effective they are and the type of biofuel they produce.</p>\n<p>Make a conclusion based on this data.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246782,
     "content_html": "The highest efficiency is Escherichia coli producing ethanol."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246781,
     "content_html": "Fatty acids are the most common biofuel produced by these organisms."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246783,
     "content_html": "Alcohols (ethanol, butanol and others ending with -ol) are the most common biofuel produced by these organisms."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246780,
     "content_html": "Zymomonas mobilis can successfully produce ethanol or 2, 3-butanediol."
    }
   ],
